Z||000005||Seanh||08-19-2001||08:00 PM||||The filter gets wet, and some of the water may be getting sucked into the engine when you start it. I don't see any harm except the annoying site of it. Unless the filter is sitting under water I doubt enough water is getting in there to cause any problems like washing the oil off the cylinder walls or somthing. I doubt you have anything to worry about.||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||08-19-2001||09:40 PM||||the scoop on side of my kit is ducted straight into filter canister, so when it rains im sure water gets in it. unless its really a lot I wouldnt worry. Back years ago people even added water injection similar to NOS system to boost HP. I do use a K&N, because the water would destroy an OEM paper filter.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=11878523&p=52990885"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||MooCow||08-19-2001||11:04 PM||||Can then I will leave it.  I am glad cause I can feel and hear a diffence when it is setup this way.  I  just had to make sure I wasn't going to ruin anything.  Now all I have to do is re-set my timming cause after I installed this my engine never really gets warm anymore and will sit at 1,500 RPM's forever.  Before I did it it would idle at 1,000 so I will get that fixed.<P>Thanks Ken||||reg||14
